For the purposes of this Regulation, the following definitions apply:

[TABLE]
(1) | ‘environmental objective’ means one of the environmental objectives laid down in Article 9 of Regulation (EU) 2020/852;
[/TABLE]
(1)
‘environmental objective’ means one of the environmental objectives laid down in Article 9 of Regulation (EU) 2020/852;

[TABLE]
(2) | ‘Taxonomy-aligned economic activity’ means an economic activity that complies with the requirements laid down in Article 3 of Regulation (EU) 2020/852;
[/TABLE]
(2)
‘Taxonomy-aligned economic activity’ means an economic activity that complies with the requirements laid down in Article 3 of Regulation (EU) 2020/852;

[TABLE]
(3) | ‘transitional economic activity’ means an economic activity that complies with the requirements laid down in Article 10(2) of Regulation (EU) 2020/852;
[/TABLE]
(3)
‘transitional economic activity’ means an economic activity that complies with the requirements laid down in Article 10(2) of Regulation (EU) 2020/852;

[TABLE]
(4) | ‘enabling economic activity’ means an economic activity that complies with the requirements laid down in Article 16 of Regulation (EU) 2020/852;
[/TABLE]
(4)
‘enabling economic activity’ means an economic activity that complies with the requirements laid down in Article 16 of Regulation (EU) 2020/852;

[TABLE]
(5) | ‘taxonomy-eligible economic activity’ means an economic activity that is described in the delegated acts adopted pursuant to Article 10(3), Article 11(3), Article 12(2), Article 13(2), Article 14(2), and Article 15(2), of Regulation (EU) 2020/852, irrespective of whether that economic activity meets any or all of the technical screening criteria laid down in those delegated acts;
[/TABLE]
(5)
‘taxonomy-eligible economic activity’ means an economic activity that is described in the delegated acts adopted pursuant to Article 10(3), Article 11(3), Article 12(2), Article 13(2), Article 14(2), and Article 15(2), of Regulation (EU) 2020/852, irrespective of whether that economic activity meets any or all of the technical screening criteria laid down in those delegated acts;

[TABLE]
(6) | ‘taxonomy-non-eligible economic activity’ means any economic activity that is not described in the delegated acts adopted pursuant to Article 10(3), Article 11(3), Article 12(2), Article 13(2), Article 14(2) and Article 15(2), of Regulation (EU) 2020/852;
[/TABLE]
(6)
‘taxonomy-non-eligible economic activity’ means any economic activity that is not described in the delegated acts adopted pursuant to Article 10(3), Article 11(3), Article 12(2), Article 13(2), Article 14(2) and Article 15(2), of Regulation (EU) 2020/852;

[TABLE]
(7) | ‘asset manager’ meansan undertaking that is subject to the disclosure obligations laid down in Articles 19a and 29a of Directive 2013/34/EU and is either of the following: (a) an AIFM as defined in Article 4(1), point (b), of Directive 2011/61/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council (4); (b) a management company as defined in Article 2(1), point (b), of Directive 2009/65/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council (5); (c) an investment company authorised in accordance with Articles 27, 28 and 29 of Directive 2009/65/EC and that has not designated for its management a management company authorised in accordance with Articles 6, 7 and 8 of that Directive. | (a) | an AIFM as defined in Article 4(1), point (b), of Directive 2011/61/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council (4); | (b) | a management company as defined in Article 2(1), point (b), of Directive 2009/65/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council (5); | (c) | an investment company authorised in accordance with Articles 27, 28 and 29 of Directive 2009/65/EC and that has not designated for its management a management company authorised in accordance with Articles 6, 7 and 8 of that Directive.
(a) | an AIFM as defined in Article 4(1), point (b), of Directive 2011/61/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council (4);
(b) | a management company as defined in Article 2(1), point (b), of Directive 2009/65/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council (5);
(c) | an investment company authorised in accordance with Articles 27, 28 and 29 of Directive 2009/65/EC and that has not designated for its management a management company authorised in accordance with Articles 6, 7 and 8 of that Directive.
[/TABLE]
(7)
‘asset manager’ meansan undertaking that is subject to the disclosure obligations laid down in Articles 19a and 29a of Directive 2013/34/EU and is either of the following:

[TABLE]
(a) | an AIFM as defined in Article 4(1), point (b), of Directive 2011/61/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council (4);
[/TABLE]
(a)
an AIFM as defined in Article 4(1), point (b), of Directive 2011/61/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council (4);

[TABLE]
(b) | a management company as defined in Article 2(1), point (b), of Directive 2009/65/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council (5);
[/TABLE]
(b)
a management company as defined in Article 2(1), point (b), of Directive 2009/65/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council (5);

[TABLE]
(c) | an investment company authorised in accordance with Articles 27, 28 and 29 of Directive 2009/65/EC and that has not designated for its management a management company authorised in accordance with Articles 6, 7 and 8 of that Directive.
[/TABLE]
(c)
an investment company authorised in accordance with Articles 27, 28 and 29 of Directive 2009/65/EC and that has not designated for its management a management company authorised in accordance with Articles 6, 7 and 8 of that Directive.

[TABLE]
(8) | ‘financial undertaking’ means an undertaking that is subject to the disclosure obligations laid down in Articles 19a and 29a of Directive 2013/34/EU and is an asset manager, a credit institution as defined in Article 4(1), point (1), of Regulation (EU) No 575/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council (6), an investment firm as defined in Article 4(1), point (2), of Regulation (EU) No 575/2013, an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 13, point (1), of Directive 2009/138/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council (7), or a reinsurance undertaking as defined in Article 13, point (4) of Directive 2009/138/EC;
[/TABLE]
(8)
‘financial undertaking’ means an undertaking that is subject to the disclosure obligations laid down in Articles 19a and 29a of Directive 2013/34/EU and is an asset manager, a credit institution as defined in Article 4(1), point (1), of Regulation (EU) No 575/2013 of the European Parliament and of the Council (6), an investment firm as defined in Article 4(1), point (2), of Regulation (EU) No 575/2013, an insurance undertaking as defined in Article 13, point (1), of Directive 2009/138/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council (7), or a reinsurance undertaking as defined in Article 13, point (4) of Directive 2009/138/EC;

[TABLE]
(9) | ‘non-financial undertaking’ means an undertaking that is subject to the disclosure obligations laid down in Articles 19a and 29a of Directive 2013/34/EU and is not a financial undertaking as defined in point (8);
[/TABLE]
(9)
‘non-financial undertaking’ means an undertaking that is subject to the disclosure obligations laid down in Articles 19a and 29a of Directive 2013/34/EU and is not a financial undertaking as defined in point (8);

[TABLE]
(10) | ‘taxonomy-aligned insurance or reinsurance activity’ means an insurance or reinsurance activity that complies with the criteria laid down in Sections 10.1 and 10.2 of Annex II to Delegated Regulation (EU) 2021/2139.
[/TABLE]
(10)
‘taxonomy-aligned insurance or reinsurance activity’ means an insurance or reinsurance activity that complies with the criteria laid down in Sections 10.1 and 10.2 of Annex II to Delegated Regulation (EU) 2021/2139.

The following requirements shall apply for the disclosures under Article 8(2) of Regulation (EU) 2020/852:

[TABLE]
(a) | non-financial undertakings shall identify each economic activity, including a subset of transitional and enabling economic activities;
[/TABLE]
(a)
non-financial undertakings shall identify each economic activity, including a subset of transitional and enabling economic activities;

[TABLE]
(b) | non-financial undertakings shall disclose the KPIs for each economic activity and the total KPIs for all economic activities at the level of the relevant undertaking or group;
[/TABLE]
(b)
non-financial undertakings shall disclose the KPIs for each economic activity and the total KPIs for all economic activities at the level of the relevant undertaking or group;

[TABLE]
(c) | non-financial undertakings shall disclose the KPIs set out in points 1.1.1, 1.1.2 and 1.1.3 of this Annex for each environmental objective and the total KPIs for all environmental objectives at the level of the undertaking or group across all environmental objectives while avoiding double counting;
[/TABLE]
(c)
non-financial undertakings shall disclose the KPIs set out in points 1.1.1, 1.1.2 and 1.1.3 of this Annex for each environmental objective and the total KPIs for all environmental objectives at the level of the undertaking or group across all environmental objectives while avoiding double counting;

[TABLE]
(d) | non-financial undertakings shall identify the proportion of the Taxonomy-aligned economic activities and the proportion of the Taxonomy-eligible economic activities that do not meet technical screening criteria. Within a Taxonomy-eligible economic activity, non-financial undertakings shall identify the proportion of that activity that is Taxonomy-aligned;
[/TABLE]
(d)
non-financial undertakings shall identify the proportion of the Taxonomy-aligned economic activities and the proportion of the Taxonomy-eligible economic activities that do not meet technical screening criteria. Within a Taxonomy-eligible economic activity, non-financial undertakings shall identify the proportion of that activity that is Taxonomy-aligned;

[TABLE]
(e) | non-financial undertakings shall identify Taxonomy-non-eligible economic activities and disclose the proportion in the denominator of the turnover KPI of those economic activities at the level of the undertaking or group;
[/TABLE]
(e)
non-financial undertakings shall identify Taxonomy-non-eligible economic activities and disclose the proportion in the denominator of the turnover KPI of those economic activities at the level of the undertaking or group;

[TABLE]
(f) | the KPIs shall be provided at the level of the individual undertaking where that undertaking prepares only individual non-financial statements or at the level of the group where the undertaking prepares consolidated non-financial statements.
[/TABLE]
(f)
the KPIs shall be provided at the level of the individual undertaking where that undertaking prepares only individual non-financial statements or at the level of the group where the undertaking prepares consolidated non-financial statements.

For the purposes of disclosures under Article 8(1) of Regulation (EU) 2020/852, asset managers shall:

[TABLE]
(a) | disclose the KPIs for each environmental objective and for aggregated taxonomy-aligned economic activities at the level of the relevant undertaking or group;
[/TABLE]
(a)
disclose the KPIs for each environmental objective and for aggregated taxonomy-aligned economic activities at the level of the relevant undertaking or group;

[TABLE]
(b) | identify a subset of transitional and enabling economic activities and disclose the KPIs for aggregated economic activities at the level of the undertaking or group;
[/TABLE]
(b)
identify a subset of transitional and enabling economic activities and disclose the KPIs for aggregated economic activities at the level of the undertaking or group;

[TABLE]
(c) | provide for a breakdown of the numerator and denominator per type of investment;
[/TABLE]
(c)
provide for a breakdown of the numerator and denominator per type of investment;

[TABLE]
(d) | disclose the KPIs in relation to aggregated taxonomy-eligible economic activities;
[/TABLE]
(d)
disclose the KPIs in relation to aggregated taxonomy-eligible economic activities;

[TABLE]
(e) | disclose the proportion of taxonomy-non-eligible economic activities within the assets under management;
[/TABLE]
(e)
disclose the proportion of taxonomy-non-eligible economic activities within the assets under management;

[TABLE]
(f) | disclose the proportion in total investments of investments in exposures referred to in Article 7(1) of this Regulation;
[/TABLE]
(f)
disclose the proportion in total investments of investments in exposures referred to in Article 7(1) of this Regulation;

[TABLE]
(g) | provide the KPIs at the level of the individual asset manager where that undertaking prepares only individual non-financial statements or at the level of the group where the undertaking prepares consolidated non-financial statements.
[/TABLE]
(g)
provide the KPIs at the level of the individual asset manager where that undertaking prepares only individual non-financial statements or at the level of the group where the undertaking prepares consolidated non-financial statements.

The KPI for fees and commission income linked to services associated with Taxonomy-aligned economic activities of undertakings, shall be defined as a proportion of the credit institution’s fees and commission income from undertakings, derived from products or services other than lending associated with Taxonomy-aligned economic activities, compared to the total fees and commission income from undertakings from products or services other than lending.
Credit institutions shall disclose the fees and commission income linked to services provided other than lending and asset management, including the following services (as reported by institutions in accordance with template 22.1 ‘Fee and commission income and expenses by activity’ set out in Implementing Regulation (EU) No 680/2014):

[TABLE]
(a) | issuance or other services related to third party securities;
[/TABLE]
(a)
issuance or other services related to third party securities;

[TABLE]
(b) | reception, transmission and execution on behalf of customers of orders to buy or sell securities;
[/TABLE]
(b)
reception, transmission and execution on behalf of customers of orders to buy or sell securities;

[TABLE]
(c) | merger and acquisition undertakings advisory services;
[/TABLE]
(c)
merger and acquisition undertakings advisory services;

[TABLE]
(d) | undertakings finance services related to capital market advisory for undertakings clients or other;
[/TABLE]
(d)
undertakings finance services related to capital market advisory for undertakings clients or other;

[TABLE]
(e) | private banking related fees;
[/TABLE]
(e)
private banking related fees;

[TABLE]
(f) | clearing and settlement services;
[/TABLE]
(f)
clearing and settlement services;

[TABLE]
(g) | custody and other related services;
[/TABLE]
(g)
custody and other related services;

[TABLE]
(h) | payment services;
[/TABLE]
(h)
payment services;

[TABLE]
(i) | fee and commission income for distribution of products issued by entities outside the prudential group to its current customers;
[/TABLE]
(i)
fee and commission income for distribution of products issued by entities outside the prudential group to its current customers;

[TABLE]
(j) | loan servicing activities;
[/TABLE]
(j)
loan servicing activities;

[TABLE]
(k) | foreign exchange services and international transactions.
[/TABLE]
(k)
foreign exchange services and international transactions.
The numerator of the KPI shall include the fees and commissions income as specified in Implementing Regulation (EU) No 680/2014, Annex V, paragraph 284 from services other than lending and asset management provided to undertakings, associated with Taxonomy-aligned economic activities. This shall be estimated by weighting the fees and commission income from each counterparty with the proportion of turnover and CapEx associated with Taxonomy-aligned economic activities of the undertaking contributing to the relevant environmental objective as disclosed by the undertaking in accordance with Article 8 of Regulation (EU) 2020/852. For financial undertakings, the ratio for the counterparty to be applied shall be the same as for the KPIs for these undertakings.
The denominator shall be the total amount of fees and commission income from undertakings from products or services other than lending and asset management.

Disclosure of KPIs and the methodology shall cover and be designed separately for all of the following services listed in Annex I, Section A, to Directive 2014/65/EU:

[TABLE]
(a) | investment firms’ dealing on own account activities, regardless of whether investment firms are principal traders or dealing on behalf of their clients in accordance with Section A, point (3), of Annex I to Directive 2014/65/EU);
[/TABLE]
(a)
investment firms’ dealing on own account activities, regardless of whether investment firms are principal traders or dealing on behalf of their clients in accordance with Section A, point (3), of Annex I to Directive 2014/65/EU);

[TABLE]
(b) | investment firms’ investment services and activities other than dealing on own account in accordance with Section A of Annex I to Directive 2014/65/EU, with the exception of point (3) of that Section.
[/TABLE]
(b)
investment firms’ investment services and activities other than dealing on own account in accordance with Section A of Annex I to Directive 2014/65/EU, with the exception of point (3) of that Section.
Ancillary services listed in Section B of Annex I to Directive 2014/65/EU shall be excluded from the scope of the disclosures.
